omx-contract (3.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: omx-contract 3.6.0
  * tests: every kernel of the 2.14.0 fixture is still declared by a live
    owner when one is named (#109)
  * answers-2.14.0: pitch cites an engine commit that declares the 2.12.0
    limits, and verifies (#112)
  * semver: the schema is classified, --report names the level, and every
    pull request runs it (#92); a red arm for travel-order, step and finite
    (#91)
  * Makefile: make check includes omx_param_units.h (#145)
  * param-contract: tests for the unit codes (#145)
  * param-contract: OMX_PARAM_CONTRACT_UNITS is declared here and rendered to
    omx_param_units.h (#145)
  * resource hints: every term carries an rdfs:label and the integer figures
    are xsd:integer, which lilv reads (#168)
  * tests: scratch directories are removed at exit; the LV2 inventory records
    a bundle that is no specification (#169)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 06:00:59 +0000
